==English==

===Etymology===
From their original purpose of carrying [[telegraph line]]s, first used around 1843 by [[w:William Fothergill Cooke|William Fothergill Cooke]].

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[pole]], usually [[wooden]], that carries [[telephone]] [[line]]s above a [[street]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1961|month=November|title=Talking of Trains: Aircraft on rail tracks|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=650|text=Here the protection consists of a 50lb per mile cadmium copper trip-wire mounted on short '''telegraph posts''' on both sides of the line, 4ft above rail level.}}

